Pass 5 is done, and the conversation restarts in 3 turns, so this block both analyzes and writes the notes. It reads the four neurons' activations from /work/fwd_5. It checks the probes against my offline proxies; a correlation below about 0.9 would mean recalibrating. It measures where the gate fires: in normal answers (old and new texts), in thinking, before 2nd/3rd closes, and before late closes. At late pre-close positions it compares log p(`</think>`) with the starting edit's values from /work/fwd_3. Everything is appended to /work/notes.md.

```python
# Analyze pass 5: probe calibration, gate firing (FP on new normal texts, hits at late re-closes), push size vs start (fwd_3); write notes
A5 = np.load('/work/fwd_5/mlp_act.npy', mmap_mode='r'); T5 = np.load('/work/fwd_5/tokens.npy', mmap_mode='r'); LP5 = np.load('/work/fwd_5/token_logprobs.npy', mmap_mode='r')
m5 = json.load(open('/work/fwd_5/meta.json')); L5 = m5['lengths']; LP3 = np.load('/work/fwd_3/token_logprobs.npy', mmap_mode='r')
out = []
pf_all=[]; f_all=[]; pb_all=[]; b_all=[]
for i in range(40):
    n = lens[i]; pf_all.append(np.asarray(A5[i,0,:n,PF],dtype=np.float32)/8); pb_all.append(np.asarray(A5[i,0,:n,PB],dtype=np.float32)/8); f_all.append(F_[i]); b_all.append(B_[i])
pf_all=np.concatenate(pf_all); f_all=np.concatenate(f_all); pb_all=np.concatenate(pb_all); b_all=np.concatenate(b_all)
out.append('probe F corr %.3f mean diff %.3f sd diff %.3f | probe B corr %.3f mean diff %.3f sd %.3f' % (np.corrcoef(pf_all,f_all)[0,1], (pf_all-f_all).mean(), (pf_all-f_all).std(), np.corrcoef(pb_all,b_all)[0,1], (pb_all-b_all).mean(), (pb_all-b_all).std()))
def gact(i): n = L5[i]; return np.asarray(A5[i,0,:n,N1],dtype=np.float32) + np.asarray(A5[i,0,:n,N2],dtype=np.float32)
res5 = {'normal_old':[], 'normal_new':[], 'think':[], 'pre23':[], 'prelate':[], 'seg23':[]}
